
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&#8217;re paying attention, there&#8217;s something weird going on at Apple lately.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">On the most recent MacBook Pro, the PROLED model, they put the glowing Apple logo back in the lid. The CEO, John Ternus, even commented on that in a <a href="https://www.wired.com/story/i-spent-30-minutes-with-apples-ceo-now-i-know-why-john-ternus-got-the-job/">recent interview with Steven Levy</a>, where he bragged about it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">When Siri AI released, a lot of us were complaining that it didn&#8217;t have enough third-party support and third-party app developers had their hands tied. Applying our traditional Apple thinking caps, we all figured that at the soonest we&#8217;d get a little bit more access next June, but this would take years. Yet that <a href="https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=gdk2umrf">expanded third-party access</a> is already showing up in the point release betas.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After the iPhone Duo released, a lot of people complained they wished it had Face ID. Well, the device doesn&#8217;t have hardware for that, but it does have a front-facing camera. And in the latest point release for the iPhone Duo, Apple&#8217;s turned on a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-duo-face-unlock-hands-on/">form of face identification</a>. It doesn&#8217;t work for everything because it&#8217;s not as secure as Face ID, but it is something a user can select to get to their phone more quickly.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It just seems Apple lately is a lot more nimble with their updates and responsiveness.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Maybe this is just a weird set of coincidences. But I&#8217;d like to attribute it to John Ternus. He is, after all, a product guy. And I can&#8217;t help but think that he uses and cares about these things more than Tim Cook did.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This isn&#8217;t meant to be a dig on Tim Cook. He did his job. And the company became a lot bigger and more profitable under his watch, but I&#8217;m not in it for the stock price. I&#8217;m in it for the user experience, and lately I&#8217;m noticing things.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I almost didn&#8217;t create this newsletter out of fear that I would jinx it all, but we may be entering a new phase with Apple products where things are a bit more delightful. I sure hope that&#8217;s the case.</p>
